@user-27, what version of pytorch are you using?
Exporting adaptive_avg_pool2d is supported with the params (1,1) since https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/9711. 
Also the issue with the ceil pooling discussed above should be fixed with https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/16769.

@user-29 You need to clarify what you want to do:

- If you want to install `torchvision==0.6.0` the `pip` command from [my previous comment](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/issues/2565#issuecomment-671188793) is enough.
- If you want to install `torchvision` from source you will **not** get `0.6.0`, but rather the current development version (`>= 0.8`)

> 

@user-36 
You can try reinstalling pillow==6.1(6.x could be okay), which is mentioned at https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/issues/4130#issuecomment-570452778. Installing torchvision by conda will automatically use the latest pillow(7.0). I met this problem when I used conda to install torch. But `UnsatisfiableError` is weird.
